# Individual: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-M> (Newton na Metr)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-M> "Newton Per Meter (N/m) is a unit in the category of Surface tension. It is also known as newtons per
    meter, newton per metre, newtons per metre, newton/meter, newton/metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system.
    Newton Per Meter (N/m) has a dimension of MT-2 where $M$ is mass, and $T$ is time. This unit is the standard SI unit in this
    category.
  "^^rdf:HTML)
